age": {"prompt_tokens": 7585, "total_tokens": 7585}}, "input": {"input": ["# SAP BTP Technology Updates Overview as of August 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key technology updates within SAP BTP, highlighting the importance of these updates in maintaining the platform's stability and security. The updates cover various components, including Java Server, Authorization and Trust Management Service, and SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations as of August 2025.\n\n## Java Server Updates\n\nThe Java Server component at SAP BTP has undergone several updates, including the update to Tomcat version 9.0.107 and the update to Java EE 7 Web Profile TomEE 7. These updates are crucial in maintaining the platform's stability and security, ensuring that the Java Server component remains up-to-date with the latest security fixes and features. Effective updates not only prevent security vulnerabilities but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (395, 163), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 08, 07))]\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service Updates\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service component at SAP BTP has undergone several updates, including the automatic signing key rotation for access tokens, the end-of-life for instance secret credential type, and the end-of-life for service plans. These updates are crucial in maintaining the platform's security and compliance with modern security standards, ensuring that the Authorization and Trust Management Service component remains up-to-date with the latest security features and best practices. Effective updates not only prevent security vulnerabilities but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2, 3, 4), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 08, 07))]\n\n## SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nThe SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime component at SAP BTP has undergone several updates, including the update to version 50.4.0. These updates are crucial in maintaining the platform's stability and security, ensuring that the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime component remains up-to-date with the latest security fixes and features. Effective updates not only prevent security vulnerabilities but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (346), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 08, 07))]", "# SAP BTP Platform Updates and Deprecations as of 2024-2026\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and deprecations within the SAP BTP platform, focusing on the Authorization and Trust Management Service, Pricing Service, and other related components. The information is relevant to the platform's operations from 2024 to 2026.\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service Updates\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service has undergone several updates, including the deprecation of the /check_token endpoint, the introduction of asynchronous service instance creation and update, and the change of default credential type to binding-secret. These changes aim to enhance security and improve the overall user experience. [Data: Records (2930, 1966, 1967), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 16), (2026, 01, 19))]\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service has introduced several new features, including on-request tracing, stateless pricing, and dynamic scale base types in price agreements. These updates aim to improve the pricing calculation process and provide more flexibility to consuming applications. [Data: Records (8, 9, 10), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## Deprecation of SAP Java Buildpack 1\n\nSAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment by December 31, 2025. Developers are advised to migrate their applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2 as soon as possible. [Data: Record (6), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 08), (2025, 12, 31))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded, and several changes have been made, including the provisioning of sub-attributes of emails, reduced scopes for credentials, and regular upgrades. These changes aim to improve the overall user experience and enhance security. [Data: Records (1521, 1522, 1523), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 29), (2025, 01, 29))]\n\n## Decentralized Identity Verification Updates\n\nDecentralized Identity Verification has introduced a new feature, sign revocation lists, which allows for the signing and validation of revocation lists. This update aims to enhance security and improve the overall user experience. [Data: Record (1525), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 01, 29))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on Cloud Foundry and technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Foundry Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (759, 305), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 04, 30))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry and Technology Governance\n\nThe Cloud Foundry and Technology Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (305), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 30))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Cloud Foundry and Technology Departments, established in Q2 2025, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (759, 305), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 30))]", "# SAP BTP Security and Compliance Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key departments focusing on security and compliance, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage security risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service Operational Scope\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in managing access and authentication for various services. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. Effective access management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. The service has undergone several changes, including the deprecation of the instance-secret credential type, the end-of-life for synchronous creation or update of service instances, and the automatic signing key rotation for access tokens as default. These changes are crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational security, especially in managing complex access and authentication scenarios. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (978, 979, 980, 981, 982), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 12, 31))]\n\n## Application Autoscaler Operational Scope\n\nThe Application Autoscaler at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in managing application scaling and performance. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential performance pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving performance regulations. Effective scaling not only prevents performance anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. The service has undergone several changes, including the end of support for the “Basic” HTTP Authentication scheme (basic auth) when using the Application Autoscaler Custom Metrics API for security reasons. These changes are crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational performance, especially in managing complex application scaling scenarios. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high performance standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (2538, 2539, 2540, 2541, 2542), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 12, 31))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in managing identity and access for various services. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. Effective identity management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. The service has undergone several changes, including the regional availability of Cloud Identity Services. These changes are crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational security, especially in managing complex identity and access scenarios. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (2539, 2540, 2541, 2542, 2543), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 12, 31))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of June 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, highlighting the components, environments, and features that have been enhanced or introduced. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of June 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Enhancements\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has been enhanced with the addition of 7 new content packages in April and May 2024. These packages include business and learning content, such as HR position planning and SAP S/4HANA Cloud. The updates aim to improve the user experience and operational efficiency of the system. [Data: Sources (293), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 05, 31))]\n\n## SAP Translation Hub Updates\n\nSAP Translation Hub has been updated to support the import of ABAP object lists and translation of ABAP short text objects in source languages other than English. These updates aim to improve the translation process and user experience. [Data: Sources (2802, 2803), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 01), (2024, 06, 07))]\n\n## SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Enhancements\n\nSAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing has been enhanced with new features, including the ability to maintain promotions, add custom logic for promotion master data validations, and identify last calculation-relevant changes in regular prices and promotions. These updates aim to improve the user experience and operational efficiency of the system. [Data: Sources (2804, 2805, 2806), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 06))]\n\n## Product Experience (PX) Survey for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\n\nA Product Experience (PX) survey has been introduced for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing, allowing users to provide feedback in real-time. This feature aims to improve the user experience and operational efficiency of the system. [Data: Source (2807), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 06))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Update as of June 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and enhancements to various SAP Cloud Services as of June 2024. The report highlights the new features, changes, and improvements across different components, including SAP Build Process Automation, SAP Translation Hub, SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing, and Cloud Identity Services. The information is relevant to the SAP Cloud Services ecosystem and is essential for understanding the current state of these services.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Enhancements\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has seen significant updates in June 2024, with the addition of new content packages, enhancements to the Maintain Promotions app, and the introduction of custom logic for validating promotion master data. These changes aim to improve the overall user experience and increase the efficiency of business processes. The updates are particularly relevant to organizations leveraging SAP Build Process Automation for their digital transformation initiatives [Data: Sources (293, 294), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 06, 07))].\n\n## SAP Translation Hub Updates\n\nSAP Translation Hub has received updates in June 2024, enabling the import of ABAP object lists and the translation of ABAP short text objects in source languages other than English. These enhancements aim to improve the translation process and increase the accuracy of translated content. The updates are particularly relevant to organizations leveraging SAP Translation Hub for their multilingual content management needs [Data: Sources (295, 296), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 01), (2024, 06, 07))].\n\n## SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Enhancements\n\nSAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing has seen significant updates in June 2024, with the introduction of new attributes for identifying last calculation-relevant changes in regular prices and promotions, enhancements to the Maintain Promotions app, and the introduction of custom logic for validating promotion master data. These changes aim to improve the overall user experience and increase the efficiency of business processes. The updates are particularly relevant to organizations leveraging SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing for their pricing and promotion management needs [Data: Sources (297, 298), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 06))].\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has received updates in June 2024, introducing application-specific groups and integrating SAML and OIDC logout flows. These enhancements aim to improve the overall user experience and increase the security of business processes. The updates are particularly relevant to organizations leveraging Cloud Identity Services for their identity and access management needs [Data: Sources (299, 300), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 01), (2024, 06, 05))].", "# SAP Technology Updates as of April 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes in SAP technology as of April 2024, focusing on the SAP Build Process Automation, SAP Translation Hub, and Integration Advisor components. The report highlights the importance of these updates in enhancing the functionality and usability of SAP systems, particularly in the areas of process visibility, data archiving, and software translation.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nThe SAP Build Process Automation component has seen significant updates in April 2024, including the introduction of Data Archiving Limits for visibility scenarios and the addition of 10 new content packages tailored to different lines of business. These updates aim to enhance the functionality and usability of the component, particularly in the areas of process visibility and data management. Effective use of these updates can help organizations streamline their business processes and improve operational efficiency [Data: Sources (783, 784), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 04, 08))].\n\n## SAP Translation Hub Updates\n\nThe SAP Translation Hub component has also seen notable updates in April 2024, including the introduction of ABAP short text object types for table entries and the availability of Company MLTR options in the Software Translation drop-down menu. These updates aim to enhance the translation capabilities of the component, particularly in the areas of software translation and data management. Effective use of these updates can help organizations improve the accuracy and efficiency of their translation processes [Data: Sources (3163, 3164), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 04, 08))].\n\n## Integration Advisor Updates\n\nThe Integration Advisor component has also seen significant updates in April 2024, including the introduction of a Proposal service opt-out option and the ability to filter code values in MIG editor. These updates aim to enhance the functionality and usability of the component, particularly in the areas of integration and data management. Effective use of these updates can help organizations improve the accuracy and efficiency of their integration processes [Data: Sources (3166, 3167), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 04, 06))].", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of April 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, focusing on various components and their environments, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance the SAP Business Technology Platform and SAP BTP, Neo Environment. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nThe SAP Build Process Automation component at SAP plays a pivotal role in automating business processes. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential process pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving technological standards. Effective process automation not only prevents anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (783, 3169), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 08))]\n\n## SAP Translation Hub Updates\n\nThe SAP Translation Hub component ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on translating ABAP short text object types, noted starting mid-2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex translations and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (3163, 3164), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 04, 08))]\n\n## Integration Advisor Updates\n\nThe Integration Advisor component ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on redesigning the Mapping List, noted starting mid-2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex integrations and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (3166, 3167), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 04, 08))]\n\n## SAP Conversational AI Updates\n\nThe SAP Conversational AI component ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on announcing the deprecation of the Community Edition, noted starting mid-2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex conversations and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (3690), Date_Range ((2023, 07, 05), (2023, 12, 31))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime component ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on updating the SAP BTP Operator module, noted starting mid-2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex runtime environments and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (3688), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 20), (2024, 01, 03))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of January 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, highlighting the importance of these changes in maintaining the company's operational stability and efficiency. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around January 2024.\n\n## Identity Authentication Upgrade\n\nSAP has upgraded its Identity Authentication service, enhancing its security features and capabilities. This upgrade is crucial for maintaining the integrity of SAP's systems and protecting user data. The upgrade was made available on January 4, 2024, and is considered a significant improvement over the previous version [Data: Sources (189), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 04), (2024, 01, 04))].\n\n## New Features in SAP Build Process Automation\n\nSAP has introduced new features in its Build Process Automation service, including 19 new content packages tailored to different lines of business. These updates are designed to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of SAP's operations, particularly in areas such as IT, sales, and procurement [Data: Sources (3689), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 01), (2024, 01, 01))].\n\n## Deprecation of SAP Cloud Portal Service\n\nSAP has announced the end-of-maintenance for its Cloud Portal service, version 1.0, on the Neo Environment. This version will be deprecated on January 25, 2024, and access to this service will no longer be possible [Data: Sources (3691), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 31), (2024, 01, 25))].\n\n## Tenant Security Headers Configuration\n\nSAP has introduced a new requirement for tenant security headers configuration, which must be done by June 2023. This change is designed to improve the security of SAP's systems and protect user data [Data: Sources (3692), Date_Range ((2023, 06, 01), (2023, 12, 31))].\n\n## Integration with Central Notification\n\nSAP has introduced a new feature that allows site administrators to choose whether to use the default notification mechanism or enable integration with central notification. This change is designed to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of SAP's operations [Data: Sources (3695), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 21), (2023, 12, 28))].\n\n## Menu Workpage Widgets Can Reference Contents From Workspaces\n\nSAP has introduced a new feature that allows widgets in workpages to reference content from any public or private workspace. This change is designed to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of SAP's operations [Data: Sources (3696), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 21), (2023, 12, 28))].", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and manage technological risks effectively. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## Identity Authentication Upgrade\n\nThe Identity Authentication service at SAP has been upgraded, enhancing its capabilities and security features. This upgrade is part of SAP's ongoing efforts to improve its technology infrastructure and ensure seamless user experiences. Effective identity authentication is crucial for safeguarding sensitive information and preventing unauthorized access to SAP's systems. The upgrade is expected to have a positive impact on SAP's overall security posture and user satisfaction. [Data: Sources (189), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 04), (2024, 01, 04))]\n\n## Trading Partner Management Enhancements\n\nSAP has introduced several enhancements to its Trading Partner Management service, including the ability to configure number ranges in company/trading partner profiles. These updates are designed to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of SAP's trading partner management processes, enabling the company to better manage its relationships with external partners and customers. The enhancements are expected to have a positive impact on SAP's operational efficiency and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (4021, 4022, 4023), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 23), (2023, 10, 23))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP has released several updates to its SAP Build Process Automation service, including the ability to select whether form or approval recipients can forward tasks to other users. These updates are designed to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of SAP's process automation processes, enabling the company to better manage its business operations and improve user experiences. The updates are expected to have a positive impact on SAP's operational efficiency and user satisfaction. [Data: Sources (3794, 3795), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 01), (2023, 12, 05))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of December 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, highlighting the latest features, changes, and releases across various components and environments. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of December 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone has seen several updates, including the introduction of a new language (Welsh) in the standard edition, and enhancements to access management in the advanced edition. These updates aim to improve user experience and streamline workflows. [Data: Sources (680, 681), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 26), (2024, 12, 26))]\n\n## SAP HANA Cloud Updates\n\nSAP HANA Cloud has received a new component version (2024.40) with improved features and functionality. This update is recommended for users to upgrade their instances and take advantage of the new capabilities. [Data: Sources (684, 685), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 23), (2025, 01, 08))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has seen updates to its default CIDR range for Nodes and the addition of a new region (US West (Oregon)) for enterprise accounts running on Amazon Web Services. These changes aim to improve performance and scalability. [Data: Sources (686, 687), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 23), (2024, 12, 23))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Updates\n\nSAP Document AI has received updates to its premium edition, including support for additional languages and payment advice documents in XLS and XLSX file types. These updates aim to improve the accuracy and efficiency of document processing. [Data: Sources (688, 689), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 23), (2024, 12, 23))]\n\n## SAP Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Process Automation has introduced two new functions (MINVALUE and MAXVALUE) for decisions, enhancing the capabilities of the platform. These updates aim to improve decision-making and automation. [Data: Sources (690, 691), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 23), (2024, 12, 23))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and user experience. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nThe SAP Build Work Zone has undergone several updates in 2024, including the introduction of a unified access control settings, a clickable workspace menu, and the ability to search for workpages in the navigation bar. These updates aim to enhance user experience and improve operational efficiency. The unified access control settings allow for consistent access options across all workspace screens, while the clickable workspace menu provides users with a more intuitive navigation experience. The ability to search for workpages in the navigation bar enables users to quickly find and access workpages, reducing the time spent searching for information. These updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to improving its technology offerings and enhancing user experience. [Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 23), (2024, 12, 26))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Updates\n\nSAP Document AI has also undergone several updates in 2024, including the introduction of new languages and the support for payment advice documents in XLS and XLSX file types. These updates aim to enhance the capabilities of SAP Document AI and improve user experience. The introduction of new languages enables users to process documents in multiple languages, while the support for payment advice documents in XLS and XLSX file types enables users to process a wider range of document types. These updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to improving its technology offerings and enhancing user experience. [Data: Sources (4, 5), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 23), (2024, 12, 26))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has undergone several updates in 2024, including the introduction of a new logo and the handling of third-party cookies. These updates aim to enhance user experience and improve operational efficiency. The introduction of a new logo provides users with a more modern and intuitive experience, while the handling of third-party cookies enables users to manage their cookies more effectively. These updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to improving its technology offerings and enhancing user experience. [Data: Sources (6, 7), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 22), (2024, 12, 26))]", "# SAP Technology and Innovation Overview as of 2024-12-23\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technologies and innovations, highlighting their connections and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024-12-23.\n\n## SAP Document AI Updates\n\nSAP Document AI has received several updates, including support for payment advice documents in XLS and XLSX formats, new languages for extraction using template, and overall improvements. These updates enhance the capabilities of SAP Document AI and support its integration with other SAP systems. [Data: Sources (1698, 1699), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 23), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone has received several updates, including managing access to workpages in the navigation bar, support admin capabilities, and UX improvements to the transport manager. These updates enhance the user experience and improve the functionality of SAP Build Work Zone. [Data: Sources (1691, 1692, 1693), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 26), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## SAP HANA Cloud Updates\n\nSAP HANA Cloud has received several updates, including a new component version available, default CIDR range for nodes changed, and region US West (Oregon) available. These updates enhance the capabilities of SAP HANA Cloud and support its integration with other SAP systems. [Data: Sources (1694, 1695, 1696), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 23), (2025, 05, 15))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud-based offerings and their evolution over time.\n\n## SAP Document AI Capabilities\n\nSAP Document AI is a powerful tool for automating business document processing, supporting over 40 languages and enabling the use of generative AI for large language models. Its capabilities have been expanded to include support for payment advice documents in XLS and XLSX formats, as well as additional languages for extraction using templates. [Data: Sources (1699, 1700), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 23), (2025, 03, 18))]\n\n## Cloud Integration Updates\n\nCloud Integration has seen significant updates, including the addition of customizable proxy settings for Edge Integration Cell Runtime, enhanced AS4 response handling, and streamlined push operations. These changes aim to improve the efficiency and reliability of cloud-based integrations. [Data: Sources (1216, 1217, 1218), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 16), (2025, 03, 18))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Enhancements\n\nKyma Runtime has undergone several enhancements, including the release of the Istio module, which provides a stable and reliable method for installing Istio and configuring it using the Istio custom resource. Additionally, the default CIDR range for Nodes has been changed to 10.250.0.0/16, and a new region, US West (Oregon), has been added for use with enterprise accounts running on Amazon Web Services. [Data: Sources (3779, 1695, 1696), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 06), (2025, 03, 18))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships, core attributes, and connections. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations as of 2024.\n\n## Process Visibility Capability\n\nThe Process Visibility Capability at SAP plays a pivotal role in providing real-time visibility into business processes. Its proactive approach helps safeguard SAP against potential operational pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective process visibility not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (601, 602), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 15), (2024, 05, 15))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Enhancements\n\nThe SAP Document AI component has undergone significant enhancements, including improved machine learning models for extracting invoice, payment advice, and purchase order documents. These improvements have led to better extraction results for currency, country, and date fields. Additionally, the service now supports the extraction of quantities with multipliers. [Data: Sources (3822, 3823, 3824), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 27), (2023, 11, 27))]\n\n## ABAP Environment Updates\n\nThe ABAP Environment at SAP has undergone updates, including the use of SAPUI5 version 1.117.4 for the administrator's SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and custom-built SAP Fiori apps. These updates have improved the overall user experience and functionality of the ABAP Environment. [Data: Sources (3828, 3829), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 25), (2024, 05, 16))]", "# SAP Technology and Finance Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and finance, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Technology Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Technology Department plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2023, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (372, 601), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 13), (2024, 05, 15))]\n\n## SAP Finance and Compliance\n\nThe SAP Finance Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on financial management and compliance, noted starting 2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex financial transactions and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (2956), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 05, 15))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Technology and Finance Departments, established in 2023, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2957, 2958), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 14), (2024, 05, 15))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_6ee392f8449a80ffd9564bb6db081012e2795cac1591c314a42ed4e472255fee_v2"}